A||||5||ayamnik||How do i reset the ecm on 86||||5
Z||000000||ayamnik||09-22-1999||04:31 PM||||I have an 86 Fiero and it idles at 1500+. I installed a new IAC in it. I know I have to reset the ECM. How do I reset it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-22-1999||04:40 PM||||look for a single orange wire with a weather pack connector near the battery. open the connector for half a minute and it resets the ECM with out screwing up the radio. If you can't find the connector disconnect the battery.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WisconsinGT||09-22-1999||06:07 PM||||Does this hold true for all Fiero's? I thought by just unhooking the battery cables, your fiero ECM was reset. No?||||reg||1
Z||000003||mwbackus||09-22-1999||08:46 PM||||In most cases, a new IAC valve will set a code 24 before it "learns" the new settings.  After the initial reset and training drive (with the engine at operating temp.), I just pull over to the side of the road and pop off the bat. cable again.  It seems that the radio presets and time are quite easy to manage, its never even really occured to me that it would be any sort of problem. Perhaps thats due to the limited selection of good channels in my area.. hmmmm<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000004||ayamnik||09-23-1999||11:25 AM||||I reset the Iac and drove for 40 miles at about 60mph. It didn’t help it It idle at 900  and all of a sudden up to 1500 or even 2000. When I stop at a light and have my foot on the brake my trany wont let it idle at more then 1000rpm but the car wont’s to idle higher so it dies. I replaced the IAC and TPS and some other censor that has a wiring connection to it and one vacuum tube and the injector it self. I have no vacuum licks. All this at normal temperature. Can any one help? I love my car and I cant do or think about anything when it not running good. Help||||reg||8
Z||000005||mwbackus||09-23-1999||12:18 PM||||A new IAC valve will set a code 24 (vehicle speed sensor) before it learns all the new settings. The result is exactly as you describe.  Reset the ECM again at home, and bring the bat. terminal removal wrench with you on your "training" drive (only needs to be a couple miles at 40 mph).  Carefully watch the check engine light to determine when the code 24 is set, the idle will also reveal this.  Then pull over to the side of the road and reset it once again.<P>Mike (who is begining to think that his posts are invisible)||||reg||1
